+        // Its copy in writes every texel of its one aspect before any command reads it, or a pass
+        // that clears it whole does (`shadow.rs`, `render/shadows.rs`), so it starts as its memory
+        // lies, as the other shadows of a buffer's bytes do (`storage_over_buffer`): zeros there
+        // would never be read, and the host's zeros copied into a full-screen surface's image
